#: ../../source/index.rst:5
#: 1eccfca5e5644d54b325110328f9f668
msgid "ArduPilot Rover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:16
#: 029f310043fa4342b59bf3436129b6e8
msgid "Rover is a sophisticated open-source firmware, specially designed for autopilots in **ground and water vehicles**. This firmware supports not only conventional 3 or 4 wheel configurations, but also extends to boats, sailboats, balance bots, and walking robots. This versatile system is capable of running missions entirely autonomously, which can be defined via mission planning software or manually pre-recorded by the driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:20
#: ea9c189cf9ae43acb5606cd0616b8de2
msgid "Rover is compatible with a wide variety of :ref:`supported autopilot boards <common-autopilots>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:22
#: 4049123fbfc541088e0a3c163325710c
msgid "Proudly, Rover was the winning platform at the `2013 and 2014 Sparkfun Autonomous Vehicle Competition <https://avc.sparkfun.com/>`__. However, Rover's functionality has extended far past this single event. It's being employed in numerous practical applications, including, but not limited to, agricultural automation. You can explore a few of these applications in our :ref:`Video Demos <rover-video-demonstrations>`."
msgstr ""

